---

What changed from the original compat/cfworkers:

  - The Cloudflare-Workers-style env bindings, ctx (waitUntil/DrainTimeout),
    scheduled()/queue() handlers, and the request.cf stub are removed —
    funcbox does not aim for Cloudflare Workers compatibility.
  - The handler signature is fetch(request) only (no env/ctx arguments); a
    module whose default export has no fetch is a boot error, and any other
    key on the default export (scheduled, queue, ...) is a warning, not an
    error.
  - The worker module loads through funcbox's own Loader + Entry (a bundle
    resolved by specifier) instead of a single inline Source string.
  - import.meta.env (Bun-compatible, string values only, frozen, declared
    keys only) is populated per module.
  - Node.js compat (compat/nodejs) is wired in as an optional, per-pool
    NodeCompat flag instead of being entirely unavailable.
  - A funcbox:-namespaced module loader is added for host-privileged modules
    (e.g. funcbox:internal), gated on the pool being constructed with them.
